<title>MONGOLIA: GOVERNMENT LIST.</title>
<headline>GOVERNMENT LIST.</headline>
<text>
<p>MONGOLIA GOVERNMENT LIST (970525)</p>
<p>  ***********************************************************</p>
<p>  * 19 May 97 - Preliminary results showed that Natsagiin *</p>
<p>  *		 Bagabandi, candidate of the opposition	*</p>
<p>  *		 Mongolian People's Revolutionary Party	*</p>
<p>  *		 (MPRP), had won a decisive 60.79 percent    *</p>
<p>  *		 in the presidential elections. President    *</p>
<p>  *		 Punsalmaagiin Ochirbat, candidate of the    *</p>
<p>  *		 ruling Democratic Union Coalition, collected*</p>
<p>  *		 29.8 percent of the vote.			 *</p>
<p>  ***********************************************************</p>
<p> President............................Punsalmaagiin OCHIRBAT**</p>
<p>							  (**See NOTE Above)</p>
<p>			   - - - - - - -</p>
<p> Prime Minister (took office 19 July 96).........M ENKHSAIKHAN</p>
<p>			   - - - - - - -</p>
<p>MINISTERS:</p>
<p> Agriculture &amp; Industry...........................L NYAMSAMBUU</p>
<p> Defence...........................................D DORLIGJAV</p>
<p> Education.........................................C LHAGVAJAV</p>
<p> Finance.............................................P TSAGAAN</p>
<p> Foreign Relations Health &amp;</p>
<p>   Social Affairs......................................L ZORIG</p>
<p> Infrastructure Development........................G NYAMDAVAA</p>
<p> Justice...........................................J AMARSANAA</p>
<p> Nature...........................................T ADIYASUREN</p>
<p>			  - - - - - - -</p>
<p> Speaker of the Great Hural</p>
<p>    (Parliament) (took office 18 July 96)........R GONCHIGDORJ</p>
<p> Deputy Speaker of the Great</p>
<p>    Hural (took office 24 July 96)................T. ELBEGDORJ</p>
<p>			  - - - - - - -</p>
<p> State Bank President.................Demchigjaviin MOLOMJAMTS</p>
